### Title
Pixi development environments and deprecated `dev/start` scripts

### Why
Contributors switch from the `dev/start` scripts to pixi environments. The
environments must run conda from the source checkout on every platform, and the
scripts must keep working while warning about their deprecation.

### Platforms
- [ ] Windows
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites
[pixi](https://pixi.sh/) installed and a clean checkout with no `.pixi` directory.
Open a fresh shell, not one with an active conda environment. On Windows, test
both cmd.exe and PowerShell. On macOS and Linux, test bash and zsh.

### Steps
1. Run `pixi shell -e py311-main`, then `python --version` and `conda info`.
2. Run `python -c "import conda; print(conda.__file__)"`.
3. Exit, then repeat steps 1 and 2 with `pixi shell -e py314-conda-forge`.
4. In the shell, run `echo $PYTHONPATH` (`echo %PYTHONPATH%` in cmd.exe) with
   `PYTHONPATH` unset before starting pixi, and again with it set to another path.
5. Run `pixi run -e py314-conda-forge unit` and stop it after a few tests pass.
6. Run `pixi run -e py314-conda-forge conda-init`.
7. On macOS, run `pixi shell -e py314-main` and note that it is not available.
8. Run `source ./dev/start --help` (`.\dev\start.bat /?` in cmd.exe) and then
   `source ./dev/start -n` (`.\dev\start.bat /N`). Redirect stderr to a file.
9. Repeat step 8 with `CONDA_DEV_START_NO_WARN=1` set.

### Pass criteria
The Python version matches the environment. `conda location` and
`conda.__file__` point to the checkout. `PYTHONPATH` starts with the checkout
and keeps an existing value. On Windows with `PYTHONPATH` unset, note whether the
value contains a literal `%PYTHONPATH%`: the activation uses
`%PIXI_PROJECT_ROOT%;%PYTHONPATH%`, which was not verified on Windows, and a
literal entry there should be fixed in `pyproject.toml`. The unit tests start and
`conda-init` runs.
The `main` environments are unavailable on macOS Intel (osx-64). The `dev/start`
scripts print a pending deprecation warning to stderr only, still behave as
before, and are silent with `CONDA_DEV_START_NO_WARN` set.

### Out of scope / notes
The dependency sync with `tests/requirements*.txt` is covered by
`tests/test_dev_environment.py`. The Windows activation syntax and `dev\start.bat`
warning are only checked here.
